---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Search an explicitly acquired native API artifact without acquisition

Usage: pse search api [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>

Options:
      --artifact <ARTIFACT>
  -C <checkout>
      --dependency <DEPENDENCY>
      --format <FORMAT>                Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --fields <FIELDS>                Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage
      --input <INPUT>
      --budget <BUDGET>                Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --output <OUTPUT>
      --path <PATHS>                   Restrict source paths without requiring Cargo or analyzer preparation
      --bound <BOUND>
      --package <PACKAGE>
      --glob <GLOB>
      --exclude <EXCLUDE>
      --type <TYPES>
      --tracked
      --untracked
      --changed
      --dependencies
      --include-ignored
      --hidden
      --generated
      --index
      --revision <REVISION>
      --limit <LIMIT>                  Stop after this many useful results; the default is twenty
      --all                            Examine the complete selected scope instead of using the default result limit
      --exists                         Stop after a positive witness; a negative answer requires complete examination
      --count
      --count-unit <COUNT_UNIT>        Select the population counted by an explicit count demand [possible values: matches, files, lines, entities]
      --order <ORDER>                  [possible values: arrival, deterministic]
      --cursor <CURSOR>                Continue a deterministic page under its original query/source guards
      --result-fields <RESULT_FIELDS>  Select result detail fields; source identity and coverage remain mandatory
      --group-by <GROUP_BY>            Group returned witnesses, without claiming exhaustive group counts [possible values: source, kind, name]
      --explain                        Explain the effective validated query without invoking its providers
  -h, --help                           Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Search an explicitly acquired native API artifact without acquisition

Usage: pse search api [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>


Options:
      --artifact <ARTIFACT>


  -C <checkout>


      --dependency <DEPENDENCY>


      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage

      --input <INPUT>


      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --output <OUTPUT>


      --path <PATHS>
          Restrict source paths without requiring Cargo or analyzer preparation

      --bound <BOUND>


      --package <PACKAGE>


      --glob <GLOB>


      --exclude <EXCLUDE>


      --type <TYPES>


      --tracked


      --untracked


      --changed


      --dependencies


      --include-ignored


      --hidden


      --generated


      --index


      --revision <REVISION>


      --limit <LIMIT>
          Stop after this many useful results; the default is twenty

      --all
          Examine the complete selected scope instead of using the default result limit

      --exists
          Stop after a positive witness; a negative answer requires complete examination

      --count


      --count-unit <COUNT_UNIT>
          Select the population counted by an explicit count demand

          [possible values: matches, files, lines, entities]

      --order <ORDER>
          [possible values: arrival, deterministic]

      --cursor <CURSOR>
          Continue a deterministic page under its original query/source guards

      --result-fields <RESULT_FIELDS>
          Select result detail fields; source identity and coverage remain mandatory

      --group-by <GROUP_BY>
          Group returned witnesses, without claiming exhaustive group counts

          [possible values: source, kind, name]

      --explain
          Explain the effective validated query without invoking its providers

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
